QuestGuidance.Register("en",226,{
[7201]="7004CFCE\n1\tTalk to Fasti inside the Dragonbone Inn\tFasti is inside the Dragonbone Inn, waiting to show you to a table where you can wait for Kólfith.\n2\tFollow Fasti to your table\tFasti is speaking with the owner of the tavern in order to arrange a table for you.\n3\tWait inside the Dragonbone Inn for Kólfith to arrive\tFasti told you to wait for Kólfith to arrive.\n4\tReturn to your table by the fire\tYou should return to your table in the Dragonbone Inn.\n5\tTalk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Dragonbone Inn\tA dwarf has come to your table in the Dragonbone Inn.\n6\tRemain alert for signs of trouble\tKólfith has come to the Dragonbone Inn, but his friendly demeanor has fallen away and he seems eager for a fight.\n7\tTalk to Kólfith in the Dragonbone Inn\tKólfith has come to the Dragonbone Inn, but his friendly demeanor has fallen away and he seems eager for a fight.\n8\tSurvive the confrontation in the Dragonbone Inn\tKólfith has come to the Dragonbone Inn, seeking to punish you for asking about Karazgar. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n9\tTalk to Ránnvig in the Dragonbone Inn\tRánnvig, the proprietor of the Dragonbone Inn, has some words for you.\n10\tTalk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Dragonbone Inn\tAuthi Gem-cutter is in the Dragonbone Inn, and he wishes to speak to you.\n",
[7202]="70059AD4\n1\tTalk to Durin in the forgotten chamber\tDurin stands in the forgotten chamber deep beneath Gundabad, boiling with rage.\n2\tRemain on your guard\tDurin has asked you to remain alert for any sign of danger.\n3\tTalk to the strange dwarf\tThe dwarf claiming to be Mótsog says he can show Durin what he has forgotten.\n4\tWitness the visions granted by the stranger\tThe dwarf claiming to be Mótsog has promised to show Durin forgotten sights.\n5\tWitness the visions granted by the stranger\tThe dwarf claiming to be Mótsog has promised to show Durin forgotten sights.\n6\tTalk to Mótsog\tIt cannot be denied that Mótsog possesses a curious power. How can he reveal these visions to you?\n7\tWitness the visions granted by Mótsog\tMótsog has promised to show Durin forgotten sights.\n8\tWitness the visions granted by Mótsog\tMótsog has promised to show Durin forgotten sights.\n9\tTalk to Mótsog\tIt cannot be denied that Mótsog possesses a curious power. How can he reveal these visions to you?\n10\tWitness the visions granted by Mótsog\tMótsog has promised to show Durin forgotten sights.\n11\tWitness the visions granted by Mótsog\tMótsog has promised to show Durin forgotten sights.\n12\tTalk to Mótsog\tIt cannot be denied that Mótsog possesses a curious power. How can he reveal these visions to you?\n13\tWitness the visions granted by Mótsog\tMótsog has promised to show Durin forgotten sights.\n14\tWitness the visions granted by Mótsog\tMótsog has promised to show Durin forgotten sights.\n15\tTalk to Mótsog\tIt cannot be denied that Mótsog possesses a curious power. How can he reveal these visions to you?\n16\tWitness the visions granted by Mótsog\tMótsog has promised to show Durin forgotten sights.\n17\tWitness the visions granted by Mótsog\tMótsog has promised to show Durin forgotten sights.\n",
[7203]="70014649\n1\tTalk to Bori\tBori is just inside the door to Gundlajân. Bori is waiting to speak with you about his plan.\n2\tClear a path through the flooded tunnels to Ghân-gharâf\tThe flooded tunnels between Gundlajân and Ghân-gharâf are blocked by ancient dwarf-mechanisms and filled with all manners of dangerous beasts. Both challenges will need to be overcome.\n3\tEnter Ghân-gharâf through the unblocked passage\tBori has helped clear a passage into Ghân-gharâf, and you should now make your way through it.\n4\tTalk to Bróin\tYou have discovered Bróin in the flooded ruin of Ghân-gharâf, still alive despite his struggle with the Watcher in the Water before the Doors of Durin.\n5\tDo battle with the Watcher in the Water\tThrough secret, water-filled passages, the Watcher has returned to Ghân-gharâf to find something unexpected: adventurers who wish to challenge it.\n6\tTalk to Bróin\tBróin is weak, but you may be able to rescue him from the flooded depths before the Watcher returns in anger.\n",
[7204]="70048CDA\n1\tTalk to Aragorn on the slag hill\tAragorn is on the slag-hill as the Battle of the Morannon rages all around him.\n2\tTalk to Mithrandir on the slag-hill\tMithrandir is on the slag-hill before the Black Gate.\n3\tRemain on your guard!\t\n4\tTalk to Mithrandir on the slag hill\tMithrandir is on the slag-hill before the Black Gate.\n5\tFind Frodo on the slopes of Orodruin\tLandroval has set you down upon the slope of Mount Doom while the Eagles circle the Mountain and seek for Frodo on the far side.\n6\tTalk to Samwise Gamgee on Orodruin\tYou have found Frodo and Sam on the slope of Mount Doom, but you do not have long before the slope will be engulfed in flame!\n7\tWalk to the edge of the outcropping... there is little time to spare!\tYou must stand on the edge of the outcropping if Gwaihir and his kin are to see you!\n",
[7205]="7005F557\n1\tTalk to Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at Mîn Lorg. You have entered Mîn Lorg to confront the Iron Crown with Hersegg. You should talk to Hersegg.\n2\tFight through Mîn Lorg with Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at Mîn Lorg.\n3\tTalk to Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at Mîn Lorg. You have come to the entryway of an ancient dwelling at Mîn Lorg. You should talk to Hersegg.\n4\tFight through Mîn Lorg with Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at Mîn Lorg.\n5\tTalk to Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at Mîn Lorg. Hersegg has spied something in the distance at Mîn Lorg. You should talk to Hersegg.\n6\tRescue the dwarf captured by the Iron Crown\tHersegg can be found at Mîn Lorg. You have found an old dwarf captured by the Iron Crown at Mîn Lorg. You should rescue the dwarf.\n7\tTalk to Thrástan\tThrástan can be found at Mîn Lorg. After rescuing Thrástan from the Iron Crown at Mîn Lorg, the old dwarf seems to be struggling to speak. You should talk to Thrástan.\n8\tTalk to Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at Mîn Lorg. After helping Thrástan to his feet, you grow concerned that the Angmarim will soon return to Mîn Lorg. You should talk to Hersegg.\n9\tEscape Mîn Lorg with Hersegg and Thrástan\tHersegg and Thrástan can be found at Mîn Lorg.\n10\tTalk to Hersegg\tHersegg can be found at Mîn Lorg. After encountering a large company of Angmarim during your attempted escape, you have found the way out of Mîn Lorg blocked. You should talk to Hersegg.\n11\tDefend Thrástan from the Iron Crown\tHersegg and Thrástan can be found at Mîn Lorg. You should attempt to overcome the Angmarim of the Iron Crown barring your escape from Mîn Lorg.\n12\tTalk to Hermáth Stormhammer\tHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Mîn Lorg. To your surprise, Hermáth Stormhammer and his warriors arrived to rescue you from the Angmarim of the Iron Crown. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.\n",
[7206]="70013AF9\n1\tTalk to Bósi\tBósi is in the passage where he believes the doorway to the Heart of Fire may be found.\n2\tTalk to Bósi\tBósi is in the passage where he believes the doorway to the Heart of Fire may be found. Bósi is waiting to speak with you about searching for the doorway.\n3\tUse hail\030Use congratulate\030Use salute\tBósi believes that by hailing or congratulating the memory of the dwarf who built the Heart of Fire, you will gain access to it.\n4\tTravel with Bósi into the Heart of Fire\tBósi's guess was correct, and you have found the location of the Heart of Fire.\n5\tTravel with Bósi into the Heart of Fire\tBósi's guess was correct, and you have found the location of the Heart of Fire.\n6\tSearch the forges on the left\030Search the forges on the right\030Search the forges in the centre\tBósi has asked you to investigate the Heart of Fire, looking for Zigilburk, the mithril axe.\n7\tTalk to Bósi\tBósi is in the Heart of Fire, looking out over the majestic hidden forges.\n",
[7207]="7001B5CD\n1\tTalk to Achardor\tThe Elves of the Hidden Guard have a decision to make: to wait for Bróin to return or to bring Mazog to the gates of Dol Guldur without him.\n2\tWait for the Hidden Guard to decide what can be done\tThe Elves of the Hidden Guard deal with frustration and the wicked words of Mazog as they decide what is to be done.\n3\tTalk to Bróin\tBróin has returned, but for what purpose did he leave Gadorgar without warning?\n4\tTalk to Achardor\tAchardor is waiting to speak with you about the upcoming exchange of Mazog for the dwarf-prisoners.\n5\tTravel with the Hidden Guard to the gates of Dol Guldur\tThe Hidden Guard has come to the gates of Dol Guldur with the prisoner Mazog in tow.\n6\tTalk to Bróin\tBróin is leaning on a walking-stick, waiting to speak with you.\n7\tTalk to Achardor\tAchardor has asked to speak with you before you proceed to the gate.\n8\tTalk to Bróin\tBróin is down the hill from Achardor and the rest of the Hidden Guard.\n9\tTalk to Achardor\tAchardor is up the hill from Bróin.\n10\tStand by the Hidden Guard as the Gate-keeper considers the offer\tThe gate-keeper of the gates of Dol Guldur is considering the offer.\n11\tTalk to Cúcheron\tThe Hidden Guard stands ready at the gates of Dol Guldur, waiting for the return of the Gate-keeper.\n12\tFollow the Hidden Guard beyond the gate\tThe Gate-keeper has called you past the gate of Dol Guldur to discuss the exchange of Mazog for the dwarf-prisoners.\n13\tTalk to Gorothúl\tGorothúl has emerged from the fortress to negotiate the exchange of Mazog for the dwarf-prisoners.\n14\tTalk to Achardor\tAchardor is concerned about the terms of the deal as presented by Gorothúl.\n15\tTalk to Achardor\tAchardor is trying to decide what can be done.\n16\tContinue the negotiations\tGorothúl has used his powers to freeze you in place, as he did before Zabadgathol.\n17\tSurvive and escape, if you can\tThe exchange has been a failure, and you must escape...if you can!\n18\tTalk to Bróin\030Talk to Cúcheron\030Talk to Sigileth\tThe Hidden Guard has fled from the gates of Dol Guldur to regroup at Ost Galadh, its errand a failure.\n",
[7208]="7000A8AA\n1\tEnter Barad Tironn and search for the palantír\tThe palantír is somewhere within Barad Tironn. You must find the palantír and steal it before Amarthiel can use it to learn the location of Narchuil.\n2\tAmarthiel and the palantír are within Barad Tironn. Laerdan has confronted Amarthiel, and now you are waiting for his command to seize the palantír and carry it from Barad Tironn. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\t\n3\tUse Palantír\tThe palantír is on its pedestal deep within Barad Tironn. Laerdan has given you the word: one of you must seize the palantír and carry it to Calenglad at the entrance of Barad Tironn! Hurry! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tDeliver the palantír to Calenglad at the entrance to Barad Tironn\tCalenglad is at the entrance to Barad Tironn. You must protect the carrier of the palantír and see it delivered to Calenglad at the entrance to Barad Tironn. Hurry!\n",
[7209]="7006C674\n1\tTalk to Agalûnu\tYou have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. You should talk to Agalûnu.\n2\tLook at the beauty of Arwáth\tYou have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. You should stop and appreciate the beauty of the grove with Agalûnu.\n3\tTalk to Agalûnu\tYou have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. Agalûnu wants to talk to you.\n4\tTalk to Agalûnu\tYou have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. Agalûnu wants to talk to you.\n5\tTalk to Shanthar\tYou have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. Shanthar has something to say to Agalûnu.\n6\tListen to the conversation\tYou have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. You should listen to their conversation.\n7\tTalk to Agalûnu\tYou have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. Agalûnu wants to talk to you.\n8\tListen to the conversation\tYou have led Agalûnu to Shanthar's abode in the wooded grove of Arwáth. You should listen to their conversation.\n",
[7210]="7000F0CB\n1\tTalk to Sverri\tSverri is standing at the doors before the great throne of Durin. The doorkeeper of Durin's throne room is waiting to speak with you about some matter.\n2\tTalk to Durin VI\tDurin VI, Lord of Moria, is waiting at the dais on the north side of the great throne room. Durin is waiting to speak with you about some matter before the Elves from Lórien arrive.\n3\tTalk to Melkólf Stonecarver\tMelkólf Stonecarver is on the west side of Durin's throne room. Durin has asked you to commission a statue of his son Náin from Melkólf Stonecarver.\n4\tTalk to Durin VI\tDurin VI is by the dais in the great throne room. You should return to Durin and tell him that Melkólf Stonecarver has agreed to make a great statue for Durin's son Náin.\n5\tTalk to Sverri\tSverri is at the front entrance to the throne room, south of Durin's great dais. Durin has asked you to speak with Sverri and await the party of Elves from Lórien.\n6\tTalk to Náin\tNáin is at the doors that enter Durin's throne-room, with the party of Elves from Lórien. Náin is waiting to speak with you.\n7\tTalk to Durin VI\tDurin VI is at the dais at the north end of the throne-room. Náin has asked you to tell Durin, his father, that the host of Elves from Lothlórien has arrived.\n8\tWait for Durin VI to finish addressing the Elves\tDurin VI is addressing the Elves from Lothlórien.\n9\tTalk to Durin VI\tDurin VI is at his dais on the north side of the throne-room. Durin is eager to impress the Elves from Lothlórien with the glory of the mithril mines.\n10\tTalk to Durin VI\tDurin VI is standing with the party in the deep caverns beneath Khazad-dûm. Durin is waiting to speak with you.\n11\tDefeat cave-claws and deep-claws (total: 7)\tDurin VI is standing with the party in the deep caverns beneath Khazad-dûm. Durin is waiting for you to clear the cavern of cave-claws and deep-claws.\n12\tTalk to Durin VI\tDurin VI is standing with the party in the deep caverns beneath Khazad-dûm. Durin is waiting to speak with you.\n13\tFollow Durin VI and his company\tDurin VI and his party is walking to the mithril deposits in the caverns deep beneath Khazad-dûm.\n14\tHelp break through the cracked wall\tDurin VI is standing with the party in the deep caverns beneath Khazad-dûm. Durin is waiting for you to help break through the cracked wall beneath Khazad-dûm.\n15\tSurvive!\tSome great terror has slumbered beneath Khazad-dûm for a long age.\n16\tEscape!\tThe dwarves are fleeing from the great terror that has been awakened beneath Khazad-dûm!\n17\tTalk to Náin, Lord of Moria\tNáin is standing with what remains of the party in the deep caverns beneath Khazad-dûm. Durin has been slain by the terrible creature that slept beneath Khazad-dûm, and now Náin is the ruler of the dwarf-kingdom.\n",
[7211]="7004A386\n1\tTalk to Captain Lachír\tTalk to Captain Lachír while you wait for his men to return.\n2\tClean off the artifact\tHelp clean off the encrusted object in front of Captain Lachír.\n3\tWait with Captain Lachír\tWait with Captain Lachír for his men to return.\n4\tDefend yourselves from Captain Lachír's men\tSomething has come over Captain Lachír's men and they are attacking without regard.\n5\tTalk to Captain Lachír\tThere is a pause in the onslaught. Captain Lachír wishes to speak.\n6\tDefend yourselves once more\tMore of Captain Lachír's men are attacking.\n",
[7212]="70010048\n1\tFind Narmeleth\tLaerdan searches even now for his beloved daughter Narmeleth, seeking to bring her the shards of Narchuil and restore her mind.\n2\tSurvive Amarthiel's onslaught\tLaerdan has been tricked. He must defend himself against the onslaught of Amarthiel, Champion of Angmar....\n",
[7213]="70066D82\n1\tTalk to Tarneth\tTarneth has travelled to an islet on Lake Evendim.\n2\tFollow Tarneth\tTarneth has travelled to an islet on Lake Evendim. You should follow her and explore the islet.\n3\tLook around at the wreck on the small islet on Lake Evendim\030Examine the wreck on the small islet on Lake Evendim\tThe wreck is located on the southern end of the islet on Lake Evendim.\n4\tTalk to Tarneth\tTarneth has travelled to an islet on Lake Evendim.\n5\tConfront Naegir\tNaegir has ambushed you at the islet on Lake Evendim.\n6\tDefeat Naegir and the wreck-hunters\tNaegir and the wreck-hunters have attacked you! You must defeat them.\n7\tTalk to Tarneth\tTarneth has travelled to an islet on Lake Evendim.\n8\tWitness Tarneth's meeting with the Blue Lady\tGwindeth, the Blue Lady, has appeared in the waters of Lake Evendim.\n9\tTalk to Tarneth\tTarneth is preparing to travel back to Tinnudir.\n",
[7214]="7003177A\n1\tTalk to Fastred\tFastred is standing just outside his father's gravesite with Framferth. Fastred wishes to speak to you about his people and his father's legacy.\n2\tWalk with Fastred\tFastred is walking through his father's gravesite.\n3\tConfront Crúmgam\tCrúmgam stands at the eastern side of Dagred's Grave. The darkening of the sky has heralded the arrival of a fierce Man of Mordor, Crúmgam. You and Fastred should confront this Man.\n4\tTalk to Fastred\tFastred is standing outside Dagred's Grave. Having defeated the Orcs brought to his father's grave by Crúmgam, you should return to Snowbourn with Fastred.\n",
[7215]="70026EFD\n1\tTalk to Elain\tThe Feast of the Running Stag is about to begin.\n2\tJoin the Stag-clansmen and observe the rites\tYou should perform the /sit emote near the bonfire to observe the festival.\n3\tObserve the Feast of the Running Stag\tThe Feast of the Running Stag has begun.\n4\tObserve the ritual as it unfolds\tYou should observe the Feast of the Running Stag.\n5\tBring the Elder what he asks for\tThe Elder's ritual crown can be found at the doorway from which he entered. You should collect the crown and carry it carefully to the Elder.\n6\tBring the Elder what he asks for when he is finished speaking\tThe Elder's ritual horse-tail can be found at the doorway from which he entered. You should collect the horse-tail and carry it carefully to the Elder when he is done speaking.\n7\tBring the Elder what he asks for when he is finished speaking\tThe Elder's ritual spear can be found at the doorway from which he entered. You should collect the spear and carry it carefully to the Elder when he is done speaking.\n8\tObserve the rites\tThe Feast of the Running Stag continues.\n9\tListen to the Elder\tThe Elder has called an early end to the Feast of the Running Stag this year, due to likely danger in the south where some of his people live.\n10\tTalk to Elain\tElain is at the Feast of the Running Stag. You should speak with Elain about the injured crow and the missing southern family.\n",
[7216]="7000F9E8\n1\tTalk to Frodo Baggins\tFrodo is on the porch of the House of Elrond, preparing to depart with the Company. The folk of Elrond's house bid farewell to the Company as they prepare to depart.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn\030Talk to Samwise Gamgee\030Talk to Meriadoc Brandybuck\tMembers of the Company can be found in front of the House of Elrond, preparing to depart. The folk of Elrond's house bid farewell to the Company as they prepare to depart.\n3\tTalk to Boromir\tBoromir stands proudly before the House of Elrond, preparing to depart with the Company. The folk of Elrond's house bid farewell to the Company as they prepare to depart.\n4\tTalk to Gandalf\tGandalf is before the House of Elrond, preparing to depart with the Company. The folk of Elrond's house bid farewell to the Company as they prepare to depart.\n5\tTalk to Elrond\tElrond is before his house, watching the Company depart. The Company is now on their way into the wild on an errand of secrecy upon which rest the hopes of all the Free Peoples.\n",
[7217]="7003A2CB\n1\tTalk to Ellen Fremedon\tEllen Fremedon can be found outside the Mead Hall of Underharrow. You have arrived in Underharrow and should acquaint yourself with Ellen Fremedon and her family.\n2\tWalk with Ellen Fremedon\tEllen Fremedon can be found around Underharrow. You have asked to speak more with Ellen Fremedon, and she is now telling you of the burdens that fall on Underharrow.\n3\tTalk to Ellen Fremedon\tEllen Fremedon can be found near the river Snowbourn in Underharrow. You have finished speaking to Ellen Fremedon and met her daughter. You should now aid her in helping the people of Rohan.\n",
[7218]="7003177F\n1\tTalk to Winsig\tWinsig stands just outside Walstow. The town is under siege by the Orcs of the East Wall. You should speak to Winsig and begin your assault.\n2\tFollow Winsig into Walstow\tWinsig is in Walstow. Nearby homes have been set ablaze by Orcs, and Winsig hopes to keep her town from ruin.\n3\tDefend the first stable of Walstow\tThe first stable lies just to the west of the Mead Hall of Walstow. Winsig hopes to keep the Orcs from slaying the steeds of her people.\n4\tFollow Winsig to the second stable\tThe second stable lies to the south of the Mead Hall of Walstow. In the wake of seeing so many steeds slain, Winsig hopes to protect any that remain alive.\n5\tDefend the second stable of Walstow\tThe second stable lies to the south of the Mead Hall of Walstow. Winsig requires your aid in defending the stable from the vicious assault of the Orcs.\n6\tCross the bridge with Winsig\tThe bridge of Walstow passes through the middle of the town. While you defeated the Orcs at the second stable, the rest of the town has burst into flame. Winsig desires to reunite with her men and put out the fires.\n7\tDefeat Gadhumúrz\tGadhumúrz stands just beyond the bridge of Walstow. Winsig must reunite with her men, but a menacing Orc blocks your path.\n8\tFollow Winsig to the Mead Hall\tThe Mead Hall lies in north-east Walstow. Winsig has called for aid from her men, and they now endeavour to put out the fires now that the Orc force is broken.\n9\tTalk to Winsig\tWinsig is standing outside the Mead Hall of Walstow. The Orc force has been repelled, and Winsig and her people are free, at least for the moment, from the danger that consumed their home.\n",
[7219]="70044312\n1\tDefeat enemies at Jal Kepir (total: 5)\tStay close to Tolwin and Dúneth and defeat enemies at Jal Kepir.\n2\tFind The First Blade\tCross the bridge to Cair Andros and find The First Blade.\n3\tDefeat Korpûrta\tDefeat The First Blade.\n4\tSpeak with Dúneth\tYou should speak with Dúneth.\n",
[7220]="7004E641\n1\tCatch up to Durin at the bottom of the stairs\tThe fortress of Skarháld is under attack! Durin raced ahead and already engages in battle at the bottom of the stairs.\n2\tTalk to Durin in the upper courtyard of the fortress\tDurin fights against the onslaught of dragon-kind at the upper courtyard of the fortress and needs your help.\n3\tClimb the central platform and assist the dwarves operating the siege defences\tDurin has seen that the dwarves operating the siege defences are in need of help, and asked you to attend to them.\n4\tTalk to Durin in the upper courtyard of the fortress\tThe drakes and other dragon-kind have begun to overwhelm Skarháld. Durin calls for you to help him turn the tide.\n5\tFight alongside Durin at Skarháld\tBótuz Frostblood fights among his people in an upper courtyard of the fortress, but the drakes and other dragon-kind do not relent.\n6\tTalk to Durin in the courtyard at Skarháld\tDurin is in the courtyard of Skarháld. Most of the dragon-kind army has retreated.\n",
[7221]="7004554F\n1\tTalk to Ingbert\tIngbert is on the Pelennor Fields just ahead of you. You have begun your foray from King's End to discover the Enemy's new commander and should now talk to Ingbert.\n2\tBattle across the Pelennor Fields\tIngbert is battling on the Pelennor Fields. Ingbert has asked you to join him in searching for the Enemy's new commander.\n3\tStand back as Duilin and Derufin clear a path\tDuilin and Derufin are scouting ahead and attempting to slay the Mûmakil. You should stand back and allow them to weaken the beasts before proceeding.\n4\tFlee to safety in the Orc encampment!\tThe Orc encampment is ahead. Duilin and Derufin have been slain by the Haradrim and their Mûmakil. You should flee into the nearby Orc encampment.\n5\tReach the Hillock with Ingbert\tThe Hillock lies to the south-east of Minas Tirith. Ingbert has decided that the best course is to reach the Hillock and make a stand against the Enemy's reinforcements there. You should follow him.\n6\tAid Imrahil and his Swan-knights\tImrahil and his Swan-knights can be found to the north of the Hillock on the Pelennor Fields. Imrahil is under attack! You and Ingbert should come to his aid.\n7\tReach the Hillock with Imrahil and Ingbert\tThe Hillock is due south of your position. Ingbert and Imrahil have begun their journey to the Hillock. You should accompany them.\n8\tDefeat Orolang\tOrolang is standing at the cross-roads to the north of the Hillock. You have found your path blocked by a dreadful wraith and must defeat him if you are to reach the Hillock.\n9\tTalk to Imrahil\tImrahil is at the cross-roads to the north of the Hillock. You should speak to him about what is to be done.\n",
[7222]="70046C4A\n1\tListen to Anborn's tale\tFaramir, Anborn, and Frodo came to the overlook of Henneth Annûn. You should listen to Anborn's tale.\n2\tListen to Anborn's tale\tAnborn and Frodo travelled down to the Forbidden Pool. You should listen to Anborn's tale.\n3\tListen to Anborn's tale\tWith Frodo's aid, Anborn hopes to capture Gollum at the Forbidden Pool. You should listen to Anborn's tale.\n",
[7223]="70037C0F\n1\tApproach the ford\tFallen men are scattered upon the ground at the Fords of Isen. You should search the men on the ground.\n2\tFallen men are scattered upon the ground at the Fords of Isen. You should search the men on the ground.\t\n3\tAsk the dying soldier what happened while you were gone\tAn injured soldier lies ahead at the river's edge. You should run to the injured man's side.\n4\tDefeat enemies at the Ford (total: 10)\tFight your way to Grimbold at the Ford.\n5\tFind Grimbold amongst the chaos\tSearch for Grimbold among the chaos at the ford.\n6\tTell Grimbold no\tGrimbold stands at Prince Théodred's grave at the Fords of Isen. You should tell Grimbold no. NOTE: This quest requires emotes. Select your target and perform the desired emote.\n7\tTell Grimbold that it is over\tGrimbold stands at Prince Théodred's grave at the Fords of Isen.\n8\tAsk the soldiers what they wish to do\tThe soldiers have gathered around Grimbold and yourself. You should ask the soldiers what they think.\n9\tSee what the soldiers choose to do\tGrimbold is at the Fords.\n10\tFollow the other soldiers in retreat\tThe men have retreated backwards into the Westfold, and you should follow.\n11\tBeckon to Grimbold\tGrimbold is still standing at Théodred's grave. You should beckon to Grimbold. NOTE: You should select your target to perform this emote.\n",
[7224]="70028B65\n1\tDefeat the Orc-smiths of Saruman (total: 12)\030Defeat the Uruk-hai Slave-masters (total: 7)\030Defeat the Master of the Forge\tEnemies in the employ of Saruman can be found throughout the Forges of Isengard.\n",
[7225]="700544ED\n1\tEnter further into Roz Dagalur, the Fiend-house\t\n2\tDefeat Bortharak\030Defeat Manargoth\030Defeat Gámgrish\030Defeat Úghurn\tDefeat the gaunt-men.\n3\tRead the notes on the altar\tRead the notes on the altar.\n",
[7226]="70034C18\n1\tSpeak with Cyneberg\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n2\tWalk with Cyneberg to the funeral\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n3\tListen to Gárwig speak\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n4\tJoin Gárwig near the twins' graves\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n5\tListen to Gárwig speak of Edsig and Gárferth\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n6\tJoin the others at Cynegar's grave\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n7\tListen to Gárwig speak about Cynegar\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n8\tPick up the stone for Cynegar's grave\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n9\tPlace the final stone on Cynegar's grave\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n10\tJoin Gárwig near the grandson's graves\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n11\tListen to Gárwig speak of Humbald and Grimgar\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n12\tJoin and watch those gathered for Gársig\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n13\tListen to Gárwig speak about Gársig\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n14\tPick up the stone for Gársig's grave\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n15\tPlace the final stone on Gársig's grave\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n16\tJoin and watch those gathered for Thrymm\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n17\tListen to Gárwig speak about Thrymm\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n18\tPick up the stone for Thrymm's grave\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n19\tPlace the final stone on Thrymm's grave\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n20\tLeave the funeral with Cyneberg\tEvery living member of Gárwig's family has come to the graveyard today to pay their respects and say good-bye to those they loved.\n",
[7227]="7004A1D0\n1\tBeckon the leaders of Fushaum Bal to come forward\tBeckon the leaders of Fushaum Bal to come forward.\n2\tMeet with the divided leaders of Fushaum Bal\tMeet with the divided leaders of Fushaum Bal.\n3\tDefend yourself!\tDefend yourself.\n4\tDefeat the leaders of Fushaim Bal.\t\n5\tTalk to Mâlatuk\tTalk to Mâlatuk.\n",
[7228]="700011AA\n1\tTalk to Lorniel\tProtect Lorniel as she searches for her father, Golodir.\n2\tOpen the gate for Lorniel\tUse the lever on the other side of the gate. As you progressed deeper into Rhunendin, you encountered a gate the key to Carn Dûm would not open. You should make your way to the lever and open the gate for Lorniel.\n3\tTalk to Lorniel\tProtect Lorniel as she searches for her father, Golodir.\n4\tTalk to Lorniel\tProtect Lorniel as she searches for her father, Golodir.\n5\tDefeat Mordirith, the False King\tAfter you found Golodir, Lorniel was slain. Now the False King stands before you, far from his source of power. Now is the time to defeat Mordirith.\n6\tTalk to Golodir\tGolodir is waiting to talk to you. You have found Golodir and driven off Mordirith, but at a terrible cost.\n",
[7229]="70029A3E\n1\tTalk to Ordwaer\tEscort Ordwaer to the gates of Isengard.\n2\tTalk to Ordwaer\tSpeak with Ordwaer before the gates of Isengard.\n3\tObserve Ordwaer's challenge\tObserve the confrontation between Ordwaer and Saruman.\n4\tConvince Ordwear to persist\tOrdwaer's nerve appears near to broken beneath the power of Saruman's voice. Speak with him and try to bolster his resolve.\n5\tObserve Ordwaer's challenge\tObserve Ordwaer's confrontation with Saruman.\n6\tTalk to Ordwaer\tSpeak with Ordwaer about his conversation with Saruman.\n",
[7230]="7006826E\n1\tTalk to Corudan outside Lhanuch\tAfter a lengthy journey, Corudan and your other companions stand outside the village of Lhanuch.\n2\tEnter Lhanuch and climb the hill\tCorudan encouraged you to climb the hill into Lhanuch and ensure that your group will be welcome.\n3\tTalk to Suvulch in Lhanuch\tSuvulch stands partway up the hill in Lhanuch.\n4\tFind Nona up the hill near the summit of Lhanuch\tSuvulch told you Nona is further up the hill within Lhanuch, and will be delighted to see you.\n5\tTalk to Nona by the fire near the summit of Lhanuch\tNona sits by the fire near the summit of Lhanuch.\n6\tStand beside the fire with your friends\tIt is a reunion of friends and adventurers near the summit of Lhanuch, but not everyone is welcome.\n7\tTalk to Nona and keep her from once again becoming Wadu's Ghost\tNona is prepared to become Wadu's Ghost and slay her former lover... but you cannot stand idly by.\n8\tStand beside the fire with your friends\tYou prevented Nona from becoming Wadu's Ghost... but it was a close thing.\n9\tSit by the fire and reminisce about your adventures\tNona has called for you and the others to sit and reminisce about your adventures.\n10\tReminisce about your adventures\tYou and your friends sit by the fire and reminisce about your shared adventures.\n",
[7231]="70068270\n1\tTalk to Corudan outside Lhanuch\tAfter a lengthy journey, Corudan and Caebar stand outside the village of Lhanuch.\n2\tEnter Lhanuch and climb the hill\tCorudan encouraged you to climb the hill into Lhanuch and ensure that your group will be welcome.\n3\tTalk to Suvulch in Lhanuch\tSuvulch stands partway up the hill in Lhanuch.\n4\tFind Nona up the hill near the summit of Lhanuch\tSuvulch told you Nona is further up the hill within Lhanuch, and will be delighted to see you.\n5\tTalk to Nona by the fire near the summit of Lhanuch\tNona sits by the fire near the summit of Lhanuch.\n6\tStand beside the fire with your friends\tIt is a reunion of friends and adventurers near the summit of Lhanuch.\n7\tExamine the gift you and Corudan worked with Caebar to prepare\tNona has set down the gift you and Corudan worked with Caebar to prepare.\n8\tStand beside the fire with your friends\tNona is grateful for the gift you and Corudan worked with Caebar to prepare.\n9\tSit by the fire and reminisce about your adventures\tNona has called for you and the others to sit and reminisce about your adventures.\n10\tReminisce about your adventures\tYou and your friends sit by the fire and reminisce about your shared adventures.\n",
[7232]="7001557E\n1\tDestroy accursed armourers (total: 5)\030Defeat the Cargûl Forge-master\tYou must destroy the accursed armoursmiths, as well their wraith master, to dispel the evil they have woven about this ancient forge.\n2\tUse the ancient anvil\030Collect Infused Sapphire\tUse the ancient forge to empower your infused sapphire.\n",
